@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam ArrowColor #59636E
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam titleFontSize 24
skinparam titleFontColor #223139
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #FAF7F0
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #314047
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #A5AFB4
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FAF7F0
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F8E9D6
skinparam noteBorderColor #D8B794
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
hide footbox
title Integrated flow — one order, six cooperating patterns
participant OrderService as Service
participant MenuCatalog as Menu
participant ToppingCatalog as Toppings
participant "Order.Builder" as Builder
participant OrderProgress as Progress
participant OrderObserver as Observer
participant ReceiptDocument as Document
participant ReceiptRenderer as Renderer

note over Service
Selected calls; HTTP, session and storage omitted.
Item/topping calls repeat for each requested item.
end note

group Create and price the order
Service -> Builder : new Builder() + configuration
Service -> Menu : create(menuItemId)
note right of Menu
Factory Method: MenuCatalog selects MealFactory;
create() delegates to createMeal().
end note
Service -> Toppings : add(meal, toppingId)
note right of Toppings
Decorator: returns a Meal wrapper.
end note
Service -> Builder : addItem(line); build()
note right of Builder
Builder creates Order; its constructor calls
PricingCalculator.calculate(...), which invokes
DiscountStrategy.discount(...).
end note
Builder --> Service : immutable Order
end

group Notify subscribers
Service -> Progress : subscribe(customer); subscribe(kitchen); announce()
Progress -> Observer : onStatusChanged(PLACED) for each subscriber
Observer --> Progress : OrderNotification
Service -> Progress : advance() on explicit demo action
note right of Progress
advance() validates the next status,
then notifies the same subscribers again.
end note
end

group Render a receipt — Bridge
note over Document, Renderer
CustomerReceipt or KitchenTicket uses either
TextReceiptRenderer or HtmlReceiptRenderer.
end note
Service -> Document : render(order, status)
Document -> Renderer : render(ReceiptContent)
Renderer --> Document : formatted String
Document --> Service : formatted String
end
@enduml
